Fake outbox bound (kurtbruns/demo.getkestrel.dev#6)

What: the fake transport's in-memory outbox and idempotency map (src/providers/fake.ts)
and the fake notifier's outbox (src/notify/fake.ts) keep only their newest entries: 500
messages each, and 5000 idempotency keys.

Why: they are module state. In local dev and Kestrel's tests the process is short-lived
and the specs clear them, but the demo runs the fake transport in production, in
long-lived isolates shared by many visitors' sandboxes, where they would grow without
bound. Nothing reads them over HTTP outside dev mode (/api/dev/outbox is dev-only), so
this is a memory bound, not a privacy fix. Dedup within the key window is best-effort:
the window is shared by every sandbox in an isolate, and a missed dedup only adds a
duplicate row to the fake outbox, never a second delivery record (those are per recipient
in the sandbox's SQLite).

See DESIGN.md, "Module-level state in Kestrel" and "The patch set".

